    "origin": "",
    "establishes": "Cause title and case number are now established from the court's own cause list at PROC-DEL-002: Shakeel Abbas v. Union of India and Ors., W.P.(CRL) 2127/2026, listed 22 July 2026 before the Chief Justice and Justice Tejas Karia. That resolves both conflicts this record used to carry. Verdictum's cause title was right; LiveLaw's date of '23 July 2026 (Wednesday)' was wrong on its own terms, since 23 July was a Thursday and the matter was listed on Wednesday the 22nd. LiveLaw's Umesh Kumar v. Delhi Police is a different petition, most likely one of the connected matters all three reports describe; which petitions were heard together is still not established. The directions below (notice to Delhi Police and the Union, preservation of records including CCTV footage and videography in accordance with the SOP in place, four weeks for a counter affidavit, and the 11 September 2026 listing) still rest on three news reports and stay CORROBORATED. A cause list does not say what was ordered. See OQ-004 for the order itself.\n\nMOVED TO DISPUTED, 18 September 2026, on retrieving the order itself (PROC-DEL-004). The order in W.P.(CRL) 2127/2026 dated 22 July 2026 dismisses the petition and contains no notice, no preservation direction, no four-week counter affidavit and no 11 September listing. It is also about a different incident: the 18 July removal of Sonam Wangchuk, which is separate from the 20 and 21 July action against students.\n\nNot resolved by preferring the order. Four outlets reported a hearing on the police action at Jantar Mantar, and one element they reported (the BNSS s.173 observation) is in this order, so they were not describing a different day's work entirely. The likeliest reading is that a direction made in another matter before the same bench was attached to this case number in the reporting, but the archive holds no such matter and will not name one it has not seen. OQ-053 asks which proceeding, if any, carries the preservation direction.\n\nThis record is the archive's own warning arriving: CORROBORATED meant four independent outlets agreeing, and four outlets agreeing about a court order is corroboration of the reporting only.",
