    "establishes": "Saket Gokhale asked four Delhi hospitals a narrow question and two answered it. The archive credits him by name because attribution is how this project treats work it did not do, and because a document obtained by an identified person under a statute is worth more than an anonymous account. What it establishes: that ten people were treated for injuries the hospitals themselves categorised as pellet or projectile injuries, on that date, at those two hospitals. Hospital records are independent of both the police and the petitioners, which is why this sits at CORROBORATED while the question of what was fired stays DISPUTED at INC-DEL-005. What it does not establish: who or what caused the injuries. 'Pellet/projectile' is a clinical category that says nothing about a weapon or about who fired it. It does not say the police fired anything, and it does not distinguish plastic from metallic. It establishes that people arrived at hospital with those injuries on the day of the police action. At least ten. AIIMS refused (OVR-DEL-002) and Ram Manohar Lohia Hospital had not replied when this was reported. The number is a floor set by which hospitals chose to answer, and the archive states it as one. Not held: the replies themselves. No outlet reproduces them. Obtaining copies would move this to VERIFIED, and it is one of the few claims here where that is straightforwardly achievable: see OQ-047.",
