    "establishes": "The claim is widely repeated, but no source fetched for this file states the place, time and manner of the arrest in terms. The Quint (20 February 2016) says the Vice-Chancellor was criticised for not following protocol before police were allowed onto the campus, and gives no date. Onmanorama (15 February 2016) reports a JNU status report saying a letter was sent to police asking them to take utmost precautions before entering the campus, and that police told the university they would enter only if absolutely necessary. Search-result snippets, which were not read as pages, describe a plainclothes arrest from the campus and raids on hostels on 12 and 13 February; they are not relied on. Not found: a police arrest memo, the case diary entry, or a court record of the place of arrest.",
